    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_dkn_121'), 'A teammate adds a dependency, which changes `package.json` and `package-lock.json`, and builds this stage:

```dockerfile
FROM node:24-slim AS build
WORKDIR /app
COPY package.json package-lock.json ./
RUN npm ci
COPY tsconfig.json ./
COPY src ./src
RUN npm run build && npm prune --omit=dev
```

Nothing under `src/` and nothing in `tsconfig.json` changed.

Statement: "`COPY tsconfig.json ./` and `COPY src ./src` run again in this build, even though the files they copy did not change."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. Each layer is built on top of the previous one, so a step can only be reused when every step before it in the stage was reused too. The first COPY misses because the lock file changed; from that point every following step runs again, including the two COPY steps whose files are unchanged. The common misconception is that Docker checks each step on its own. That is exactly why the rarely changing inputs go first and the often changing ones (src/) go last.', 3, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_dkn_121') AND order_index = 3)
