    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_dkn_131'), 'The incident review found this line in the api Dockerfile. Since then, the staging compose file sets its own `DATABASE_URL`:

```dockerfile
FROM node:24-slim
WORKDIR /app
ENV NODE_ENV=production
ENV DATABASE_URL=postgres://rice:Pr0d-pass@prod-db.internal:5432/rice_rocket
COPY --from=build /app/dist ./dist
CMD ["node", "dist/server.js"]
```

```yaml
# compose.staging.yml
services:
  api:
    image: registry.example.com/rice-rocket/api:1.4.0
    environment:
      DATABASE_URL: postgres://rice:stg-pass@staging-db:5432/rice_rocket
```

Statement: "Now that staging sets `DATABASE_URL` at run time, the production password can no longer be read by anyone who can pull the image."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. `ENV` is written into the image configuration. A run-time value only shadows it inside that one container; the image still carries the production URL, and `docker image inspect` (or `docker history`) prints it for anyone who can pull the image. The common misconception is that overriding a variable removes it. The fix is to delete the line, rebuild, and rotate the password, because every image already pushed keeps it.', 1, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_dkn_131') AND order_index = 1)
