-- challenge chal_coding_dkn_132 (mini_coding)
INSERT INTO challenge.challenges (public_id, course_id, module_id, lesson_id, name, title, description, status, difficulty, type, points, is_published, is_deleted)
VALUES ('chal_coding_dkn_132', (SELECT id FROM catalog.course WHERE public_id = 'docker-nginx-ship-a-service'), (SELECT id FROM course.module WHERE course_id = (SELECT id FROM catalog.course WHERE public_id = 'docker-nginx-ship-a-service') AND order_index = 1 AND is_deleted = false LIMIT 1), (SELECT id FROM course.lesson WHERE content_source = 'lesson-dkn-1-3' AND is_deleted = false LIMIT 1), 'load-config-from-env', 'Fail fast on a bad environment', 'Assemble `loadConfig(env, files)` for the api: it runs once at startup and either returns the whole configuration or stops the container with every problem listed. `env` is an object like `process.env` (strings or undefined; a variable set to "" counts as not set). `files` maps a path to its content and stands in for the files mounted in the container, such as Docker secrets under /run/secrets/.

Rules: PORT is decimal digits only, from 1 to 65535, default 3000 (returned as a number). DATABASE_URL is required and must start with postgres:// or postgresql://. LOG_LEVEL is one of debug, info, warn, error, default info. The JWT secret comes from JWT_SECRET, or from the file whose path is in JWT_SECRET_FILE with its trailing line break (\n or \r\n) removed; setting both is an error, and an empty secret counts as missing.

Collect every problem, then throw ONE Error whose message is the problems sorted alphabetically (plain `sort()`) and joined with "; ". The exact problem texts: `PORT must be an integer from 1 to 65535, got "<value>"` · `DATABASE_URL is required` · `DATABASE_URL must start with postgres:// or postgresql://` (never echo the URL: it holds the password) · `LOG_LEVEL must be one of debug, info, warn, error, got "<value>"` · `JWT_SECRET or JWT_SECRET_FILE is required` · `JWT_SECRET and JWT_SECRET_FILE are both set` · `JWT_SECRET_FILE not found: <path>`.

Without problems, return a frozen object `{ port, databaseUrl, logLevel, jwtSecret }`. Run shows `{ ok: true, frozen, config }` or `{ ok: false, errors }`, where errors is your message split on "; ". The editor holds the finished function with its blocks missing, each marked by a `// [ ]` line: fill every line with a piece. Some pieces are wrong on purpose, so check each one against the rules above.', 'open', 'medium'::difficulty_question, 'mini_coding', 30, true, false)
