WITH q AS (
    INSERT INTO challenge.questions (challenge_id, question, type, explanation, order_index, points)
    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_dkn_151'), 'The api runs with `restart: unless-stopped`; two hours into a Postgres outage:

```text
$ docker compose ps --format ''table {{.Service}}\t{{.Status}}''
SERVICE   STATUS
api       Up 2 hours (unhealthy)
db        Restarting (1) 12 seconds ago

$ docker inspect --format ''{{.RestartCount}}'' rice-rocket-api-1
0
```

Statement: "If the outage lasts long enough, `restart: unless-stopped` makes Docker restart the unhealthy api container."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. A restart policy on plain Docker Engine and Compose reacts to the container''s process exiting; the health status does not trigger it, which is why the api is `Up 2 hours (unhealthy)` with RestartCount 0. Something else has to act on unhealthy: Swarm replaces unhealthy tasks, and tools like an autoheal container restart them. The misconception is that `unhealthy` plus a restart policy equals self-healing; restarting the api would not bring Postgres back anyway.', 3, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_dkn_151') AND order_index = 3)
    RETURNING id
)
