WITH q AS (
    INSERT INTO challenge.questions (challenge_id, question, type, explanation, order_index, points)
    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_dkn_161'), 'The forwarded headers are set at server level, and the reports location adds one header of its own:

```nginx
server {
    proxy_set_header Host              $host;
    proxy_set_header X-Real-IP         $remote_addr;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For   $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;

    location /api/reports/ {
        proxy_set_header Connection "";
        proxy_read_timeout 300s;
        proxy_pass http://api/reports/;
    }
}
```

Statement: "Requests to `/api/reports/` still carry `X-Real-IP` and `X-Forwarded-Proto`, because the location only adds one more header."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. proxy_set_header directives are inherited from the outer level only if the current level defines none. The single `proxy_set_header Connection ""` in the location replaces the whole inherited set, so report requests reach the api with only the defaults (Host $proxy_host) plus Connection: the api sees nginx''s IP and http again for exactly these requests. People read it as "add one more"; nginx reads it as "this level has its own list". Repeat the four headers in the location, or move the extra header to server level.', 2, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_dkn_161') AND order_index = 2)
    RETURNING id
)
