VALUES ('chal_coding_dkn_162', (SELECT id FROM catalog.course WHERE public_id = 'docker-nginx-ship-a-service'), (SELECT id FROM course.module WHERE course_id = (SELECT id FROM catalog.course WHERE public_id = 'docker-nginx-ship-a-service') AND order_index = 3 AND is_deleted = false LIMIT 1), (SELECT id FROM course.lesson WHERE content_source = 'lesson-dkn-3-1' AND is_deleted = false LIMIT 1), 'nginx-reverse-proxy-default-conf', 'Fix the api proxying in default.conf', 'Since nginx went in front, the api logs every client as 172.18.0.5, `/api/orders` reaches it as `/api/orders` (404, the api''s routes have no /api prefix), redirects point to http:// and report exports fail with 504 after 60 s. Assemble the fixed default.conf: (1) `/api/...` reaches the api (api:3000, an `upstream api` block is recommended) without the `/api` prefix, query string kept; everything else stays with the static app; (2) every request to the api carries `Host` (the public host name), `X-Real-IP` (the client IP), `X-Forwarded-For` and `X-Forwarded-Proto` (the scheme the client used, http or https); (3) `/api/reports/` waits 300 s for the api (`proxy_read_timeout 300s`) while every other api request keeps the 60 s default. Run grades it with a routing simulator: for each request it reports where nginx sends it, the path the api receives, the forwarded headers and the read timeout. The editor starts from the finished file with key blocks missing (`[ ] label` lines): fill each one by clicking a piece, or drag it onto the line on desktop. Some pieces are wrong on purpose.', 'open', 'medium'::difficulty_question, 'mini_coding', 30, true, false)
