    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_dkn_171'), 'The web app is a single-page app. Its build output and the location that serves it:

```text
/usr/share/nginx/html/index.html
/usr/share/nginx/html/assets/index-4f9a2c.js
```

```nginx
location / {
    try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;
}
```

Statement: "A request for `/orders/42` gets `index.html` with status 200, and the address bar still shows `/orders/42`, so the app''s router can render order 42."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. Neither the file /orders/42 nor a directory /orders/42/ exists, so try_files makes an internal redirect to its last parameter, /index.html. An internal redirect happens inside nginx: the browser receives the shell with 200 and never sees a new URL, so the client-side router reads /orders/42. The misconception is that this is an HTTP redirect (301/302); it is not, and that is exactly why deep links work.', 2, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_dkn_171') AND order_index = 2)
    RETURNING id
)
