WITH q AS (
    INSERT INTO challenge.questions (challenge_id, question, type, explanation, order_index, points)
    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_dkn_181'), 'The deploy switches the upstream from blue to green while a 4-minute report export is running on blue:

```text
10:20:00  GET /api/reports/monthly  -> nginx worker 31 -> api-blue:3000   (in flight)
10:20:41  deploy: write upstream green; nginx -t ok; nginx -s reload
10:20:41  nginx: start worker processes 58, 59 (new config: api-green)
10:20:41  nginx: gracefully shutting down worker process 31
10:20:43  deploy: smoke test green ok; drain blue 300s ...
```

Statement: "The export that is in flight on worker 31 finishes on api-blue, and only new requests go to api-green."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. On reload the master starts new workers with the new configuration and asks the old ones to shut down gracefully: they stop accepting new connections but finish the requests they already serve, against the config they started with (api-blue). That is why the script must keep blue running for a drain period at least as long as the slowest request before stopping it. The misconception is that a reload cuts every open connection, like a restart would.', 1, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_dkn_181') AND order_index = 1)
    RETURNING id
)
