WITH q AS (
    INSERT INTO challenge.questions (challenge_id, question, type, explanation, order_index, points)
    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_dkn_181'), 'A typo slipped into the generated upstream file during a deploy:

```nginx
upstream api {
    server api-gren:3000;
}
```

```text
$ docker compose exec nginx nginx -t
nginx: [emerg] host not found in upstream "api-gren:3000" in /etc/nginx/conf.d/upstream.conf:2
nginx: configuration file /etc/nginx/nginx.conf test failed
```

Statement: "If the script had run `nginx -s reload` anyway, nginx would have stopped serving and every request would fail until someone fixed the file."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. On reload nginx first tries to load the new configuration; if that fails it logs the error and keeps running with the old one, so traffic keeps flowing to blue. The reason to test first is different: the broken file stays on disk, and the next nginx restart (a crash, a host reboot, `docker compose up` recreating the container) cannot start at all. The deploy must treat a failed `nginx -t` as a rollback: write the blue upstream back and remove green. The misconception is that a bad reload takes the site down; the real risk is a hidden landmine for the next restart.', 2, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_dkn_181') AND order_index = 2)
    RETURNING id
)
