    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_dkn_181'), 'Release 1.8.0 passed its healthcheck but broke checkout. The deploy log:

```text
14:02:10  start green ricerocket/api:1.8.0
14:02:31  wait healthy green ... healthy
14:02:31  write upstream green; nginx -t ok; reload nginx
14:02:32  smoke test green: POST /api/checkout -> 500
14:02:32  write upstream blue; nginx -t ok; reload nginx
14:02:33  stop green
```

Statement: "The rollback takes about a second because api-blue was still running with the previous release; the script only pointed the upstream back and reloaded nginx."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. Blue is retired only after the smoke test passes and a drain period ends, so when green fails, the previous release is still running and warm. Rolling back is a file write and a reload, not a rebuild or an image pull. The common misconception is that a healthcheck is enough of a gate: it proves the process answers /health, not that checkout works, which is why the switch ends with a real-traffic check while blue still exists.', 3, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_dkn_181') AND order_index = 3)
    RETURNING id
)
