VALUES ('chal_coding_dkn_182', (SELECT id FROM catalog.course WHERE public_id = 'docker-nginx-ship-a-service'), (SELECT id FROM course.module WHERE course_id = (SELECT id FROM catalog.course WHERE public_id = 'docker-nginx-ship-a-service') AND order_index = 3 AND is_deleted = false LIMIT 1), (SELECT id FROM course.lesson WHERE content_source = 'lesson-dkn-3-3' AND is_deleted = false LIMIT 1), 'blue-green-deploy-plan', 'Plan a blue-green switch with a rollback', 'Every deploy ran `docker compose up -d api`, which stopped the old container before the new one was ready (20-40 s of 502s), and one bad release took 15 minutes to roll back by hand. Assemble `planDeploy(state, results)` for the new deploy script from the pieces. `state` is `{ active: "blue" | "green", candidateImage, drainSeconds? }` (default drain 30 s); `results` says how each gate turns out: `{ healthy, configTest, reload, smoke }` (booleans). Return `{ actions, active }`: the ordered steps, each written exactly as `start <colour> <image>`, `wait healthy <colour>`, `write upstream <colour>`, `nginx -t`, `reload nginx`, `smoke test <colour>`, `drain <colour> <n>s`, `stop <colour>`, and the colour serving traffic at the end. The happy path starts the other colour, waits for it to be healthy, writes the upstream file, tests it, reloads, smoke-tests, drains and stops the old colour. When a gate fails, the plan stops there and rolls back: the candidate is stopped, the upstream file names the old colour again, and nginx is reloaded only if it was already serving the candidate (then test the restored file first). Never reload a config that failed `nginx -t`, and never stop the old colour before the smoke test passed. The editor starts from the function with every gate missing (`[ ] label` lines): fill each one by clicking a piece, or drag it onto the line on desktop. Some pieces are wrong on purpose.', 'open', 'medium'::difficulty_question, 'mini_coding', 30, true, false)
